\ A word body's definitions live in a frame the call owns on this tier too: a `name: swap ;` local
\ read from the word's own loop body is fresh on every call whatever context reached it, and a
\ definition made in a word body is gone once the word returns, without reaching the durable
\ entry frame or the collision guards. The binary's answers must match the interpreter's for
\ tests/integration/word_body_local_frame.1z.
\
\ Every local here is read only from a quotation handed to a combinator, and every nested
\ definition is left uncalled: a word that calls its own nested definition at the body's top level
\ is not AOT-compilable, so a call would turn these pins into a build failure. The module call is
\ wrapped in `call` rather than `when`, since a top-level `when` whose quotation leaves a value
\ behind fails in a binary on its own (spec/bugs/20260904-aot-top-level-when-result.md).

use "ranges" ;
use "sequences" ;
use "fixtures/aot_word_body_local_frame_mod.1z" ;

neighbors: ( n -- vec ) [
  n: swap ;
  [ ] make-vector
  { 1 2 } [ n + #push! ] #each
] ;

[ 80 neighbors drop ] call
5 neighbors >array .
{ 30 40 } [ t [ neighbors >array ] [ drop ] if ] #map #collect .

[ 5 place ] call .
9 place .

define-inside: ( -- ) [ inside-only: ( -- n ) [ 42 ] ; ] ;
define-inside
"inside-only" defined? .

shadow-nip: ( -- ) [ nip: ( -- n ) [ 42 ] ; ] ;
shadow-nip
1 2 nip .
